[0.018, "o", "Working with an AI agent\r\nIn brief\r\nA read-only token\r\nThe contract\r\nThe envelope\r\nExit codes\r\nByte budgets\r\nText the cluster didn't write\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.094, "o", "\u001b[2m# resources (3 nodes): bun 310.0 MiB, 7.6 % CPU · nodes 1344.1 MiB, 16.4 % CPU · network 60.4 in, 60.4 out KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.073, "o", "\u001b[2m# Resource use: 73 samples over 360 s on 3 nodes, added together\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#                      average           peak\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   bun CPU                8.6 %         26.2 %\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   bun memory           377.2 MiB      428.7 MiB\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   node CPU              33.7 %        186.0 %\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   node memory         1531.9 MiB     1759.6 MiB\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   network in           407.3 KiB/s  14801.5 KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   network out          180.1 KiB/s   3036.8 KiB/s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m#   CPU is a percentage of one core.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# That's the tour. `relish local destroy --yes` removes the cluster,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# and `relish uninstall` removes relish itself.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# New in 0.3.0: the same cluster on real machines. `sudo relish netboot` installs our\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# appliance OS on them over the network; https://reliaburger.com/#netboot shows how.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# New in 0.3.3: `relish apply --wait` returns once every app is ready, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# `relish apps NAME` lists each instance's sidecars under it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.022, "x", "0"]
